      "id": "GENUS_TAMANDUA",
      "name": "Tamandua",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Tamanduas — medium-sized, semi-arboreal anteaters with a prehensile tail that functions as a fifth limb for gripping branches. Tamanduas are equally comfortable in trees and on the ground, raiding both arboreal termite nests and ground-level ant colonies. Like the giant anteater, they have a body temperature several degrees lower than most mammals (around 33°C) and lack teeth entirely. They produce a powerful, skunk-like musk from anal glands when threatened. Tamanduas are more widespread and common than the giant anteater, tolerated in disturbed habitats and secondary forest.",
      "lineage": "Tamanduas",
