      "id": "GENUS_CYCLOPES",
      "name": "Cyclopes",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "The silky anteater — the world's smallest anteater, barely larger than a human fist at 17 cm body length and 175–400 grams. It is almost entirely arboreal and nocturnal, rarely if ever descending to the ground, and feeds almost exclusively on arboreal ant species. Camouflaged to resemble a seed pod of the silk-cotton tree (Ceiba), where it commonly shelters, the silky anteater can be astonishingly difficult to see even when pointed at it. When threatened, it adopts a boxing posture, raising its forelegs to protect its face. Largely unstudied due to its secretive, arboreal lifestyle.",
      "lineage": "Silky Anteater",
